<!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
<div class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Global Intentional Homicide Trends:<br>A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023)</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of intentional homicide rates across countries, sexes, and age groups over three decades, drawing on United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) data.</p>
    <p class="meta">Generated: 7 May 2026 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Data source: UNODC Crime Trends Survey &nbsp;|&nbsp; 201 countries &amp; territories &middot; 22,092 observations</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- ===== KPI DASHBOARD ===== -->
<div class="kpi-dashboard" id="kpi-dashboard"></div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: GLOBAL OVERVIEW ===== -->
<section id="global-overview">
  <h2 class="section-title">1. Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
  <p class="section-obj">Present the overall global trend in homicide rates from 1990 to 2023 and assess whether the world is becoming safer.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Global Median &amp; Mean Homicide Rate Over Time</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:420px;"><canvas id="chartGlobalTrend"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Key Observations</h3>
      <div id="global-observations"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Reporting Coverage Over Time</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:280px;"><canvas id="chartCoverage"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box info">
    <strong>Critical caveat:</strong> The global mean is sensitive to which countries report in a given year. The <strong>median</strong> provides a more robust central tendency measure in this unbalanced panel. All global aggregates should be interpreted with an understanding that the set of reporting countries shifts year to year.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: REGIONAL COMPARISON ===== -->
<section id="regional-comparison">
  <h2 class="section-title">2. Regional &amp; Country-Level Comparison</h2>
  <p class="section-obj">Identify the countries and regions with the highest and lowest homicide rates and discuss geographic patterns.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Regional Median Homicide Rates (2023)</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:340px;"><canvas id="chartRegionalBar"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Regional Trends Over Time</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:380px;"><canvas id="chartRegionalTrend"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Top 10 Countries by Homicide Rate (2023)</h3>
      <table class="data-table" id="table-top10"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Country</th><th class="text-right">Homicide Rate</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Bottom 10 Countries by Homicide Rate (2023)</h3>
      <table class="data-table" id="table-bottom10"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Country</th><th class="text-right">Homicide Rate</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="regional-insights"></div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 3: GENDER DISPARITY ===== -->
<section id="sex-disparity">
  <h2 class="section-title">3. Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>
  <p class="section-obj">Analyze the difference in homicide rates between males and females globally, quantifying the male-to-female ratio and how it has changed over time.</p>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Men are <span style="font-size:1.2em;font-weight:700;" id="mf-ratio-display"></span> more likely to be victims of intentional homicide than women, based on the median country-level ratio in the most recent year. This disparity is one of the most persistent and striking patterns in the dataset.
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Male vs. Female Median Homicide Rates</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:300px;"><canvas id="chartSexTrend"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Male-to-Female Ratio Over Time</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:300px;"><canvas id="chartMFRatio"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="gender-insights"></div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 4: AGE GROUP ANALYSIS ===== -->
<section id="age-group-analysis">
  <h2 class="section-title">4. Age Group Analysis</h2>
  <p class="section-obj">Examine which age groups face the highest homicide risk and assess whether youth or elderly populations are disproportionately affected.</p>

  <div class="highlight-box info">
    <strong>Data note:</strong> Age-disaggregated homicide data are available only by sex (male/female), not as a combined total. The analysis below pools male and female age-specific records to identify which age groups carry the highest homicide risk overall.
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Median Homicide Rate by Age Group</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:320px;"><canvas id="chartAgeBar"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Age Group Trends Over Time</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-height:320px;"><canvas id="chartAgeTrend"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="age-insights"></div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 5: NOTABLE TRENDS & OUTLIERS ===== -->
<section id="notable-trends">
  <h2 class="section-title">5. Notable Country-Level Trends &amp; Outliers</h2>
  <p class="section-obj">Highlight countries with the most dramatic increases or decreases in homicide rates over the observation period.</p>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="badge badge-green">Improvement</span> &nbsp;Largest Homicide Rate Declines</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-bottom:12px;">Countries with ≥15 years of data, ranked by absolute rate reduction</p>
      <table class="data-table" id="table-decreases"><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Period</th><th class="text-right">Start</th><th class="text-right">End</th><th class="text-right">Change</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="badge badge-red">Deterioration</span> &nbsp;Largest Homicide Rate Increases</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-bottom:12px;">Countries with ≥15 years of data, ranked by absolute rate increase</p>
      <table class="data-table" id="table-increases"><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Period</th><th class="text-right">Start</th><th class="text-right">End</th><th class="text-right">Change</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </div>

